From: dj
Subject: [PATCH] PUBG v4.7+: pin UObject.Name = 0x18

PUBG Mobile scrambles FName.CompIdx at the stock UObject::Name slot, so
MobileDumper-7's Init_UObject_Name heuristic (which walks 0x08..0x58 and
scores each offset by CompIdx plausibility) can't find it. UE 4.18 ships
UObject::Name at 0x18 on 64-bit and PUBG keeps it there — just with the
real value encrypted. OverrideInGenOffsets runs BEFORE the scan and when
Offsets.UObject.Name is already set, Init_UObject_Name is skipped entirely.

--- a/Dumper/Profile/CustomProfiles/Shared/PUBG.h
+++ b/Dumper/Profile/CustomProfiles/Shared/PUBG.h
@@ -58,6 +58,20 @@
 		}
 	}

+	// PUBG Mobile scrambles FName.CompIdx at the stock UObject::Name slot, so
+	// the comparison-index heuristic in Init_UObject_Name walks past 0x58
+	// without a hit. UE 4.18 ships UObject::Name at 0x18 on 64-bit and
+	// that's where PUBG keeps it; pin it so the generator can proceed.
+	void OverrideInGenOffsets(FInGenOffsets& Offsets) const override
+	{
+#ifdef __LP64__
+		Offsets.UObject.Name = 0x18;
+#else
+		Offsets.UObject.Name = 0x10;
+#endif
+	}
+
 	void OverrideDecryptCallbacks(FDecryptCallbacks& Callbacks) const override
 	{
 		Callbacks.Statics.GNames = [](const FDecryptContext<uintptr_t>& Context)
